<%# Jobs index — TWO views of the same list, one page.
    The TABLE is the original and is unchanged: it is what the row-click script,
    the alignment tests and the preview-routing tests all read. The GRID is
    ADDED beside it, never a rewrite of it, and the two share the model's
    decisions (Job#preview_file / #preview_from_upload?) and the ONE favourite
    partial — a second copy of either is the thing that drifts.

    Both views are always rendered; #jobs-grid carries `hidden` in the markup,
    so the table is what shows with JS off. The CSS `[hidden]` guard
    (display: none !important) is what actually hides the inactive one — every
    .btn here sets its own display, which would otherwise beat the attribute's
    UA rule. %>
<div class="page-head">
  <div class="page-head-row page-head-row--split page-head-row--stacked">
    <h1 class="section-title"><span class="gradient-text">Jobs</span></h1>
    <%= link_to "Run Job", new_job_path, class: "btn btn-primary head-action" %>

  <%# #jobs-view-toggle-list-grid: which of the two views below is shown. Two
      plain buttons in a segmented box, not a select and not a link: the choice
      is a display mode, so it must not navigate and must not reload the page.
      They carry NO .head-action class on purpose — that class is the head's
      measured 2.75rem/7.325rem action box (see head_action tests), and these two
      are small paired controls, not head actions.

      The grid places them itself: the row is `1fr auto`, the title is pinned to
      row 1 col 1 and the blurb to row 2 col 1, so the auto-placed Run Job takes
      row 1 col 2 and this takes row 2 col 2 — directly under the Run Job button,
      at the right edge. Giving it an explicit row/column instead would put it in
      the SAME cell as Run Job, and squeezing it beside that button would mean
      widening the 1fr/auto grid the other seven heads share. %>
  <%# The wrapper closes inline on the last button's line, never as a line of its
      own: page_head_uniformity/responsive_head read the head row with a lazy
      /<div class="page-head-row[^"]*">.*?\n  <\/div>/m, so a line that begins
      with two spaces and </div> ends "the row" early and the blurb would be
      read as outside it. %>
  <div class="view-toggle" role="group" aria-label="Jobs view"><button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary view-toggle-btn" data-view-toggle="list" aria-pressed="true" title="List view — the table">List</button><button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary view-toggle-btn" data-view-toggle="grid" aria-pressed="false" title="Grid view — thumbnails">Grid</button></div>

  <p class="page-head-blurb page-head-blurb--long">Every run traces a raster into candidates, measures printability and pixel fidelity, then waits for you to pick. Nothing advances on its own — the trace stage stops at the menu, because choosing which candidate goes to final is a visual call a machine has no business making for you.</p>
  </div></div>

<%# #jobs-list-view: the table, wrapped so the toggle has one element to hide. %>
<div id="jobs-list">
<% if @jobs.any? %>
  <div class="tbl-wrap tbl-wrap--narrow">
    <table class="candidates">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th class="col-thumb">Preview</th>
          <th>Name</th>
          <th class="col-center">State</th>
          <th class="col-center">Passed</th>
          <th class="col-center">Runner</th>
          <th class="col-narrow" aria-label="Actions"></th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <% @jobs.each do |job| %>
          <tr class="rowlink" data-href="<%= job_path(job) %>">
            <td class="col-thumb">
              <%# Which file previews the row is the model's call (Job#preview_file
                  / #preview_from_upload?): the run's COLOUR SOURCE by default
                  (the raster it was fed -- source.png on a pipeline job), and
                  the PROOF PNG once a pick has been proved. Both live on the
                  runner, so they ride the file proxy; only a plot/blender/bp
                  drawing or a raster-only flux variation comes from uploads.
                  A file that is not there yet degrades to the matte-grey
                  scissor placeholder rather than a broken-image icon -- and
                  never hides the row. %>
              <%# A real <a>, not just the row's JS data-href: the thumbnail has
                  to be focusable, followable with the keyboard, and open in a
                  new tab on middle-click. It points at the JOB, which is also
                  what the row's data-href says -- they used to disagree, with
                  the name and thumb going to the proof while the row went to
                  the job, so clicking the name took you somewhere other than
                  the thing it is named after. One destination per row; the
                  proof is reached from the job. %>
              <a class="thumb job-thumb" href="<%= job_path(job) %>"
                 title="<%= job.name %> — open the job">
                <span class="thumb" title="<%= job.name %> — preview">
                  <% if job.preview_file.present? %>
                    <img src="<%= job.preview_from_upload? ? upload_preview_jobs_path(name: job.preview_file) : file_job_path(job, name: job.preview_file) %>"
                         alt="Preview for <%= job.name %>"
                         loading="lazy" onerror="this.parentNode.dataset.missing = '1'; this.remove();">
                  <% end %>
                </span>
              </a>
            </td>
            <td><a class="cs-job-name" href="<%= job_path(job) %>"><strong><%= job.name %></strong></a></td>
            <td class="col-center"><span class="status-pill status-<%= job.state %>"><%= job.state %></span></td>
            <td class="col-center mono" style="color:var(--success)"><%= job.passed_count %></td>
            <td class="col-center mono"><%= job.runner %></td>
            <td class="col-narrow">
              <div class="cs-row-actions">
                <% if job.state == "done" %>
                  <%# Same button the Proof control was, pointed at the archive.
                      The box was always 32x32, but the Proof control drew a
                      14x14 inline SVG while this one used a TEXT glyph -- U+1F5AB,
                      which Press Start 2P does not contain, so it silently fell
                      back to another font and drew at a different visual size
                      inside the same 32px box. Twelve rows of that reads as a
                      broken column. An inline SVG cannot fall back, so it is
                      what the Proof button had and what this one gets. %>
                  <%= link_to download_job_path(job),
                        class: "btn btn-icon cs-job-download", title: "Download 7z",
                        "aria-label" => "Download #{job.name}" do %><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M21 15v4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-4"></path><polyline points="7 10 12 15 17 10"></polyline><line x1="12" y1="15" x2="12" y2="3"></line></svg><% end %>
                <% end %>
                <% if job.in_flight? %>
                  <button type="button" class="btn btn-icon cs-job-action cs-job-cancel"
                          data-cs-job-action="cancel" data-url="<%= cancel_job_path(job) %>"
                          data-name="<%= job.name %>" title="Cancel" aria-label="Cancel <%= job.name %>">✕</button>
                <% else %>
                  <button type="button" class="btn btn-icon cs-job-action cs-job-delete"
                          data-cs-job-action="delete" data-url="<%= job_path(job) %>"
                          data-name="<%= job.name %>" title="Delete" aria-label="Delete <%= job.name %>">✕</button>
                <% end %>
              </div>
            </td>
          </tr>
        <% end %>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
<% else %>
  <div class="card empty-state">
    <p>No runs yet. Feed it a raster to get started.</p>
  </div>
<% end %>
</div>

<%# #jobs-grid-view: the same runs as cards -- one thumbnail, the name, the
    state and the passed count, plus the action icons. Deliberately LOW
    information: no runner column and no headers (the table is where you read
    those), so a card stays a picture you recognise rather than a paragraph.
    Hidden in the markup so a JS-less page shows the table, and so the default
    is 'list' without the script having to run. %>
<div id="jobs-grid" hidden>
<% if @jobs.any? %>
  <div class="job-grid">
    <% @jobs.each do |job| %>
      <%# #jobs-grid-card-preview-url: the SAME model decision the table makes,
          resolved once per card. The colour source (or a finished proof) is
          served through the runner's file proxy; a plot/blender/bp output or a
          raster-only flux variation lives in storage/uploads behind the
          login-gated upload_preview route. Job#preview_from_upload? is the
          two-sided answer, and it stays the only place that decides it. %>
      <%
        preview_file = job.preview_file
        preview_url = nil
        if preview_file.present?
          preview_url = job.preview_from_upload? ? upload_preview_jobs_path(name: preview_file) : file_job_path(job, name: preview_file)
        end
      %>
      <div class="job-card">
        <%# A real <a> to the JOB — the same destination the table's thumb and
            name use. The card is not itself clickable: the thumbnail is the
            big obvious target, and a card-wide click would fight the action
            row that sits inside it. %>
        <a class="job-card-thumb" href="<%= job_path(job) %>" title="<%= job.name %> — open the job"
           <% if preview_file.blank? %>data-missing="1"<% end %>>
          <% if preview_file.present? %>
            <%# Same onerror contract as the table's thumbnail: a file that is
                not there degrades to the matte-grey scissor placeholder instead
                of a broken-image icon. Empty when the job has produced nothing
                yet — a missing card is not an option, so the box stays. %>
            <img src="<%= preview_url %>" alt="Preview for <%= job.name %>" loading="lazy"
                 onerror="this.parentNode.dataset.missing = '1'; this.remove();">
          <% end %>
        </a>

        <div class="job-card-body">
          <a class="cs-job-name" href="<%= job_path(job) %>"><strong><%= job.name %></strong></a>
          <div class="job-card-meta">
            <span class="status-pill status-<%= job.state %>"><%= job.state %></span>
            <%# The same one number the table's Passed column carries, mono and
                green. The word "passed" is the tooltip rather than a visible
                label: with no headers on a card, a bare number needs a name
                only when you ask for it. %>
            <span class="mono job-card-passed" title="<%= job.passed_count %> passed candidates"><%= job.passed_count %></span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <%# #jobs-grid-card-actions: icons only, inline SVG at the same 14px /
            stroke-2 style as the table's buttons. Text glyphs are banned here
            for the reason the table documents: Press Start 2P does not contain
            them, so they fall back to another font and draw at a different
            visual size inside an identical box. %>
        <div class="job-card-actions">
          <%# PREVIEW — the one action every job has, and the only way into the
              site popup from this page. data-cs-view/data-cs-url/data-cs-title
              is the contract aether.js wires (~497/746); it opens the same modal
              the job page's tiles open. When there is nothing to show yet (a
              queued flux or plot run with no raster), the control stays — every
              card is the same shape — but it is disabled rather than wired to a
              URL that cannot resolve, so it can never open a broken viewer. %>
          <button type="button" class="btn btn-icon job-card-action cs-job-preview"
                  <% if preview_url %>data-cs-view="svg" data-cs-url="<%= preview_url %>"<% end %>
                  data-cs-title="<%= job.name %>"<% if preview_url.blank? %> disabled="disabled"<% end %>
                  title="<%= preview_url.present? ? "Preview #{job.name}" : "Nothing to preview yet" %>"
                  aria-label="<%= preview_url.present? ? "Preview #{job.name}" : "Nothing to preview yet" %>"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M1 12s4-8 11-8 11 8 11 8-4 8-11 8-11-8-11-8z"></path><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"></circle></svg></button>

          <% if job.state == "done" %>
            <%# DOWNLOAD — only a finished run has an archive to fetch; the
                runner's download route refuses anything else. %>
            <%= link_to download_job_path(job),
                  class: "btn btn-icon cs-job-download job-card-action",
                  title: "Download 7z", "aria-label" => "Download #{job.name}" do %><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M21 15v4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-4"></path><polyline points="7 10 12 15 17 10"></polyline><line x1="12" y1="15" x2="12" y2="3"></line></svg><% end %>

            <% if !job.flux? %>
              <%# SEND TO RUN JOB — the raster this run was traced from, handed
                  back to the Run Job form. A POST button, not a link: reuse
                  fetches source.png from the runner and files a new job, which
                  is a write. Flux jobs have no runner source.png to reuse (their
                  raster was generated, and reuse only accepts source.png /
                  source.inverse.png from a runner), so they do not get this. %>
              <%= button_to reuse_job_path(job, name: "source.png"),
                    class: "btn btn-icon job-card-action cs-job-reuse",
                    title: "Send to Run Job", "aria-label" => "Send #{job.name} to Run Job" do %><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="1 4 1 10 7 10"></polyline><path d="M3.51 15a9 9 0 1 0 2.13-9.36L1 10"></path></svg><% end %>
            <% end %>

            <%# SAVE TO SCRAPBOOK — one star, two routes. A runner-backed file
                goes through scrapbook/_fav_button (the single star and the
                single handler: it fetches the bytes through the runner). A
                generated raster has no runner file behind it, so the partial's
                handler would 502 — exactly the reason the flux page saves
                through scrapbook/save_upload instead. Same glyph, same 14px
                polygon, the route that can actually reach the bytes. %>
            <% if job.preview_from_upload? %>
              <%= button_to scrapbook_save_upload_path,
                    params: { name: job.preview_file, job_id: job.id },
                    class: "btn btn-icon job-card-action cs-job-fav",
                    title: "Favourite #{job.name} (preview)",
                    "aria-label" => "Favourite #{job.name} (preview)" do %><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><polygon points="12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2"></polygon></svg><% end %>
            <% else %>
              <%= render "scrapbook/fav_button", job_id: job.id, name: job.preview_file,
                         label: "preview", css_class: "btn btn-icon job-card-action fav-btn" %>
            <% end %>
          <% end %>

          <%# CANCEL replaces DELETE in flight, exactly as on the table: a
              running job is stopped, a finished one is removed, and the two are
              different requests (POST cancel vs DELETE job). aether.js (~821)
              reads data-cs-job-action to pick the verb, asks for confirmation
              first, and reloads. %>
          <% if job.in_flight? %>
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-icon cs-job-action cs-job-cancel job-card-action"
                    data-cs-job-action="cancel" data-url="<%= cancel_job_path(job) %>"
                    data-name="<%= job.name %>" title="Cancel <%= job.name %>"
                    aria-label="Cancel <%= job.name %>"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><line x1="18" y1="6" x2="6" y2="18"></line><line x1="6" y1="6" x2="18" y2="18"></line></svg></button>
          <% else %>
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-icon cs-job-action cs-job-delete job-card-action"
                    data-cs-job-action="delete" data-url="<%= job_path(job) %>"
                    data-name="<%= job.name %>" title="Delete <%= job.name %>"
                    aria-label="Delete <%= job.name %>"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="3 6 5 6 21 6"></polyline><path d="M19 6v14a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H7a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V6"></path><path d="M10 11v6"></path><path d="M14 11v6"></path></svg></button>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>
<% else %>
  <%# Only ever visible with the grid selected, because the list's copy of this
      card is hidden at the same moment. Two copies, one shown at a time, so the
      empty page says the same thing in either view. %>
  <div class="card empty-state">
    <p>No runs yet. Feed it a raster to get started.</p>
  </div>
<% end %>
</div>

<script>
  document.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
    if (e.target.closest('a,button,form,input,select,textarea')) return;
    var row = e.target.closest('tr.rowlink');
    if (row) window.location = row.dataset.href;
  });
</script>

<%# #jobs-view-toggle-script: the toggle's whole implementation.
    - The class on <body> is the mode, so CSS can key off it; the `hidden`
      attribute on the two wrappers is what actually swaps them.
    - localStorage keeps the choice across visits. It is read with a guard and
      written with a guard: a private-mode browser throws on both, and the page
      must still work (it just forgets).
    - The click listener is bound ONCE and DELEGATED from document, so it
      survives Turbo Drive's body swap (this script re-runs on every visit, and
      a per-visit binding would stack listeners). apply() re-runs on turbo:load
      because the swapped-in body starts in the markup's default state.
    - Default is 'list': nothing here runs and the table is already showing. %>
<script>
  (function () {
    var KEY = 'chopshop.jobsView';

    function readView() {
      try { return localStorage.getItem(KEY) === 'grid' ? 'grid' : 'list'; }
      catch (e) { return 'list'; }
    }

    function apply(view) {
      var grid = view === 'grid';
      var list = document.getElementById('jobs-list');
      var cards = document.getElementById('jobs-grid');
      if (list) list.hidden = grid;
      if (cards) cards.hidden = !grid;
      document.body.classList.toggle('jobs-view-grid', grid);
      document.querySelectorAll('[data-view-toggle]').forEach(function (btn) {
        var on = (btn.dataset.viewToggle === 'grid') === grid;
        btn.classList.toggle('is-active', on);
        btn.setAttribute('aria-pressed', on ? 'true' : 'false');
      });
    }

    function writeView(view) {
      try { localStorage.setItem(KEY, view); } catch (e) { /* forget it, show it */ }
      apply(view);
    }

    if (!window.__csJobsView) {
      window.__csJobsView = true;
      document.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
        var btn = e.target.closest('[data-view-toggle]');
        if (!btn) return;
        e.preventDefault();
        writeView(btn.dataset.viewToggle === 'grid' ? 'grid' : 'list');
      });
      document.addEventListener('turbo:load', function () { apply(readView()); });
    }

    apply(readView());
  })();
</script>
